Assets invested in the global Exchange Traded Fund (ETF) industry reached a new record high at the end of May 2025 – standing at USD16.27 trillion. In this article we consider what led the way in terms of latest trends and look at.


ETF characteristics;
Active ETFs and their associated product development journey (including disciplinary devices and regulatory considerations such as transparency and naming conventions);
ETF liquidity benefits over mutual funds;
The global spread of ETF products;
Examine the potential benefits, and possible issues, associated with dual share class ETFs;
Citi as an ETF partner; and
Look to what the future may hold.


Overall, ETFs will continue to evolve, addressing demographic trends such as the rise in digitally-savvy investors, anticipated regulatory changes, and an increased focus on wealth accumulation.
